'''Line D''' of the [[CristoCarril]] (CC) system is a commuter rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that runs on the [[Via Sud Line]] corridor between the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Els Camps (CristoCarril)|Els Camps]] in [[Els Camps]]. The line covers 64.2 km and serves 16 stations across two comarcas — [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará]]. It is the fourth CristoCarril line, complementing [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] on the [[Coastal Line]] corridor, [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] on the [[Portnou Line]] corridor, [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]] on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor, and [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] on the [[Sant Bart Line]] corridor.

Line D follows a central-southern route from the Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal, through the ciutats of Sant Cristòfor — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], and [[Ciutat del Pujol (ciutat)|Ciutat del Pujol]] — before entering the Cumará comarca and serving the municipalities of [[Brises]] and [[Els Camps]]. The line shares the first five stations with [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]] on the Sant Bart Line corridor before diverging onto the Old Grand Subdivision at Mas Blanc through central Sant Jordi, then joining the Via Sud Subdivision southward through Ciutat del Pujol and into Cumará.

== Route ==

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

Line D begins at the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], the city's primary rail hub, shared with [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]], [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]], and [[Line E (CristoCarril)|Line E]]. From the terminal, the line heads south through three stations in Original — [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]], [[Sant Pere (CristoCarril)|Sant Pere]], and [[La Font (CristoCarril)|La Font]] — serving the dense residential neighbourhoods south of the historic core. These four stations are shared with Lines B, C, and E. At La Font, Line B diverges to follow the [[Portnou Line]] corridor through [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] and [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]], while Line C continues on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor through the eastern ciutats. Lines D and E continue together on the [[Sant Bart Line]] corridor for one additional station to [[Mas Blanc (CristoCarril)|Mas Blanc]] in [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], where Line E continues north on the Sant Bart Line while Line D diverges onto the Old Grand Subdivision, heading southeast through central Sant Jordi.

The line then serves six additional stations in Sant Jordi on the Old Grand Subdivision: [[Estadi (CristoCarril)|Estadi]], [[Mercat Vell (CristoCarril)|Mercat Vell]], [[Carretera del Camp (CristoCarril)|Carretera del Camp]], [[Plaça dels Pins (CristoCarril)|Plaça dels Pins]], [[Polígon Sud (CristoCarril)|Polígon Sud]], and [[Riera Seca (CristoCarril)|Riera Seca]]. Sant Jordi is a densely populated residential ciutat on the eastern side of Sant Cristòfor, and these stations provide the primary commuter rail connection for its central and southern neighbourhoods, complementing the seven Line C stations that serve the western part of Sant Jordi.

Continuing south, the line enters [[Ciutat del Pujol (ciutat)|Ciutat del Pujol]], serving three stations: [[Turó del Pujol (CristoCarril)|Turó del Pujol]], [[Plaça del Pujol (CristoCarril)|Plaça del Pujol]], and [[Pujol Sud (CristoCarril)|Pujol Sud]]. Ciutat del Pujol is a residential ciutat on the southeastern edge of Sant Cristòfor, and these stations provide the only CristoCarril connection to the area. The 11 stations within Sant Cristòfor cover the central and southeastern districts of the city.

=== Cumará ===

After leaving Sant Cristòfor, Line D enters the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]] and serves the municipality of [[Brises]], a suburban municipality with a population of over 38,000. The line stops at [[Brises (CristoCarril)|Brises]], the municipality's sole rail station, situated on the Via Sud Subdivision between Ciutat del Pujol and Els Camps.

The line then enters the municipality of [[Els Camps]], the southernmost station on the line and the terminus. [[Els Camps (CristoCarril)|Els Camps]] station serves the municipality's principal settlement, with a population of over 52,000. The station functions as a regional rail hub for the southern Cumará communities, providing the primary commuter connection to Sant Cristòfor.

