== Service pattern ==

Line D operates three service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Els Camps]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Short''' || All stops 1–11 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Riera Seca || ~38 min
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 5, 7, 11, 14, 16 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Els Camps, skipping intermediate stations || ~50 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–16 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Els Camps || ~75 min
|}

The '''short''' service operates entirely within [[Sant Cristòfor]], running from the Central Terminal through the central and southeastern ciutats — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], and [[Ciutat del Pujol (ciutat)|Ciutat del Pujol]] — to Riera Seca on the southern edge of Sant Jordi. This is the most frequent service, providing high-capacity commuter rail for the residential districts of central and southern Sant Cristòfor.

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and Els Camps, stopping at the Central Terminal, Portal de Sant Cristòfor, Mas Blanc, Mercat Vell, Riera Seca, Pujol Sud, and Els Camps. The express skips most suburban stations within Sant Cristòfor and all intermediate stations in Ciutat del Pujol and Brises, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 50 minutes. The express is primarily used by long-distance commuters between Sant Cristòfor and the southern Cumará communities.

The '''local''' service stops at all 16 stations along the full 64.2 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 75 minutes. The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Sant Jordi (Estadi, Carretera del Camp, Plaça dels Pins, Polígon Sud), Ciutat del Pujol (Turó del Pujol, Plaça del Pujol), and Brises.

== Schedule ==

Line D operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Short''' || every 10 min || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 20 min (daytime), every 30 min (evening)
|-
| '''Express''' || every 20 min || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 30 min (daytime), every 60 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|}

The short service is the most frequent, reflecting the high commuter demand within central and southern Sant Cristòfor. The express provides a regular connection between Sant Cristòfor and Els Camps, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in outer Sant Cristòfor and Cumará. Combined, the three services provide up to 11 trains per hour at the Central Terminal during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line D uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line operates a flat fare of B$2.50 for all journeys, regardless of distance travelled.

Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

